@startuml Room-Replay-UseCases
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 9

title UpDown QnD — Room Replay Flow\nCurrent (broken) vs Correct (designed)

left to right direction

actor "Player" as player
actor "Host" as host

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' CURRENT BROKEN FLOW
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

rectangle "CURRENT FLOW (BROKEN)" as BROKEN #FFCDD2 {
  usecase "game.over\nstate='finished'" as B1
  usecase "player.clickPlayAgain\n(client-side)" as B2
  usecase "client.leaveRoom()\n← WRONG: disconnects" as B3 #EF9A9A
  usecase "client.onLeaveRoom()\nshows lobby UI" as B4
  usecase "setTimeout(500ms)\nclient.joinRoom(sameId)" as B5 #EF9A9A
  usecase "server.addPlayer()\nREJECTED: state='finished'" as B6 #EF9A9A

  usecase "PRESET ROOMS: autoRecreate\ndeletes room, creates new" as B7 #FFE082
  usecase "Race condition:\nnew room may not exist\nat 500ms" as B8 #EF9A9A
}

player --> B2
B1 --> B2 : GAME_OVER msg
B2 --> B3
B3 --> B4
B4 --> B5
B5 --> B6 : FAILS for user rooms
B1 --> B7 : preset rooms only
B7 --> B8

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' CORRECT REPLAY FLOW
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

rectangle "CORRECT FLOW (DESIGN)" as CORRECT #E8F5E9 {
  ' @uc:uuid:ea33c5b7 game.end.playAgain
  usecase "UC-GE5: game.end.playAgain\n[ea33c5b7]\nPlayer clicks 'Play Again'" as C1 #A5D6A7

  usecase "client.sendPlayAgain()\nNO leaveRoom, NO rejoin\nplayer stays connected" as C2 #A5D6A7

  usecase "server.handlePlayAgain()\nroom.votePlayAgain(playerId)" as C3 #A5D6A7

  usecase "room.resetForReplay()\n<<include>>" as C4 #A5D6A7

  usecase "reset state → 'waiting'\nreset scores/alive/hands/round\nkeep players + chat + host" as C4a #E8F5E9

  usecase "broadcast ROOM_RESET\nall clients show lobby\nwith same player list" as C5 #A5D6A7

  usecase "UC-G1: host.startGame()\n[560d9a46]\nHost starts new game" as C6 #A5D6A7

  usecase "UC-R10: player.leave()\n[96f2ecd5]\nPlayer leaves (Back to Lobby)" as C7 #A5D6A7
}

player --> C1
C1 ..> C2 : <<include>>
C2 ..> C3 : <<include>>
C3 ..> C4 : <<include>>
C4 ..> C4a : <<include>>
C4 ..> C5 : <<include>>
C5 --> C6 : host ready
host --> C6
player --> C7 : opts out

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' IMPLEMENTATION CHANGES NEEDED
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

rectangle "Implementation Changes" as IMPL #FFF3E0 {
  usecase "NEW: GameRoom.resetForReplay()\nreset state/scores/deck\nkeep connections" as I1
  usecase "NEW: MSG.PLAY_AGAIN\nclient→server message" as I2
  usecase "NEW: MSG.ROOM_RESET\nserver→client broadcast" as I3
  usecase "FIX: MultiplayerUI.renderGameOver()\nsend PLAY_AGAIN, don't leaveRoom" as I4
  usecase "FIX: endGame() for user rooms\ndon't auto-delete after 60s\nif players present" as I5
  usecase "NEW: MultiplayerUI.handleRoomReset()\nre-render lobby with existing players" as I6
}

note bottom of CORRECT
  **Design Principles:**
  P6: resetForReplay() resets model, not object
  P1: Room IS its scenario — reset scenario
  P11: No protocol knowledge in UI
  P4: Room resets itself (polymorphism)

  **What resetForReplay() does:**
  - this.state = 'waiting'
  - this.round = 0
  - this.deck = createShuffledDeck()
  - this.gmHand = []
  - this.currentCard = null
  - players.forEach: score=0, streak=0,
    alive=true, currentGuess=null,
    roundsPlayed=0, inventory=fresh
  - keep: players Map, chatHistory,
    hostId, spectators, bots
end note

note bottom of BROKEN
  **Root causes:**
  1. No PLAY_AGAIN server message
  2. Client does leave+rejoin (wrong)
  3. state='finished' blocks addPlayer()
  4. User rooms auto-delete after 60s
  5. Preset rooms delete+recreate (race)
  6. No resetForReplay() method exists
end note

@enduml
